# NASA-adapted requirement checklist

Apply this file only after authoring. Do not merge it into
[requirements-authoring.md](requirements-authoring.md). Do not persist SDoc. Do not choose models or
lineups.

This table paraphrases the public NASA SEH Appendix C concern set
(`SRC-EMV-NASA-SEH`, DEC-EMV-004). It is not the appendix, not a second
register, and not ISO 29148 clause coverage (`SRC-EMV-29148` metadata-only).
Do not copy NASA or INCOSE handbook body.

## S8 citations (DEC-EMV-003 fields relied on)

| row_id | source | issuer | edition | URL | retrieval_date | status | precedence | mismatch | derived rule | evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| SRC-EMV-NASA-SEH | NASA Systems Engineering Handbook; named Appendix C | NASA, Office of the Chief Engineer | NASA/SP-2016-6105 Rev2 | https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/nasa_systems_engineering_handbook_0.pdf | 2026-09-09 | informative | 8 | none versus DEC-EMV-002 | Paraphrase Appendix C concerns; map each to an AlphaZede rule, check type, typed failure, and evidence; do not copy body | S8 full-text PDF receipt; access_class full-text |
| SRC-EMV-COE | AlphaZede COE libraries | AlphaZede | `docs/coe/index.md` plus ELSD/ASA `.sdoc` as in S8 | repository://Alphazedehq/docs/coe/index.md | 2026-09-09 | tailored | 2 | S8 records index-pin vs worktree ELSD digest mismatch | Cite COE UIDs and CONTRACT-EMV-004; do not copy COE body; owner decisions outrank COE | S8 full-text UID grep |
| SRC-EMV-29148 | ISO/IEC/IEEE 29148:2018 RE processes and information items | ISO, IEC, IEEE | 2018 Edition 2 | https://www.iso.org/standard/72089.html | 2026-09-09 | normative | 5 | 2018 current; DIS is watch-only | Process-family citation only; invent no clauses | S8 access_class metadata-only |
| SRC-EMV-INCOSE-SEH-V5 | INCOSE SEH v5 practitioner guidance | INCOSE / Wiley | Fifth Edition, 2023 | https://www.incose.org/resources-publications/technical-publications/se-handbook/ | 2026-09-09 | informative | 7 | none versus DEC-EMV-002 v5 pin | Not used as checklist body; no INCOSE text | S8 access_class metadata-only |

Check type uses the COE-ELSD-064 set. For a statement, only inspection or
analysis applies.

## Rows

| id | concern | AlphaZede rule | check type | typed failure | evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| CHK-RE-01 | Binding language names a duty, not a hope or a fact | CONTRACT-EMV-004; SRC-EMV-COE | inspection | AMBIGUOUS_MODALITY | Quoted modal or missing duty verb |
| CHK-RE-02 | Named subject performs the action | CONTRACT-EMV-004 allocated | inspection | UNOWNED_SUBJECT | Subject string or its absence |
| CHK-RE-03 | Product or procedure form states the need | CONTRACT-EMV-004 | inspection | WRONG_FORM | Statement pattern versus subject type |
| CHK-RE-04 | Names for the subject and its parts stay stable | CONTRACT-EMV-004 precise | inspection | INCONSISTENT_NAME | Name variants in the statement or set |
| CHK-RE-05 | Quantities carry an observable bound | CONTRACT-EMV-004 measurable | inspection | UNMEASURABLE | Missing number, bound, or identity |
| CHK-RE-06 | Statement says the need, not the design | COE-ELSD-016; CONTRACT-EMV-004 | inspection | IMPLEMENTATION_SPECIFIC | Design or how-to clause in the statement |
| CHK-RE-07 | Statement is not an operator activity | COE-ELSD-016 | inspection | OPERATIONS_MIXED | Operator or activity clause |
| CHK-RE-08 | Grammar, spelling, and house style hold | CONTRACT-EMV-004 precise | inspection | EDITORIAL_DEFECT | Marked language defects |
| CHK-RE-09 | Duty is stated as a positive obligation where a prohibition is not the need | CONTRACT-EMV-004 | inspection | NEGATIVE_FORM | Unjustified prohibition |
| CHK-RE-10 | Open values have owner and close-by date | CONTRACT-EMV-004 measurable | inspection | OPEN_PLACEHOLDER | Bare placeholder with no owner or date |
| CHK-RE-11 | Rationale and assumptions are recorded | CONTRACT-EMV-004 | inspection | MISSING_RATIONALE | Empty rationale or assumption field |
| CHK-RE-12 | Statement lives in the requirement layer, not an appendix, plan, or design | COE-ELSD-016; COE-ASA-014 | inspection | WRONG_LAYER | Host artifact type versus requirement layer |
| CHK-RE-13 | One meaning; no indefinite pointer or hedge | CONTRACT-EMV-004 precise | inspection | AMBIGUOUS | Hedge or unresolved pronoun |
| CHK-RE-14 | Wording is short enough to check | CONTRACT-EMV-004 | inspection | VERBOSE | Extra clauses that do not change the duty |
| CHK-RE-15 | One obligation per statement | CONTRACT-EMV-004 precise | inspection | COMPOUND | Multiple duties or mixed rationale |
| CHK-RE-16 | One subject and one predicate | CONTRACT-EMV-004 | inspection | MALFORMED_STATEMENT | Extra subjects or predicates |
| CHK-RE-17 | Statement is complete, or the open item is tracked | CONTRACT-EMV-004 | inspection | INCOMPLETE | Missing object, bound, or tracked open item |
| CHK-RE-18 | Needed kinds of need for the scope are present or listed as gaps | CONTRACT-EMV-004; AC-EMV-009 | analysis | COVERAGE_GAP | Scope list versus statement set |
| CHK-RE-19 | Assumptions are written, not implied | CONTRACT-EMV-004 | inspection | HIDDEN_ASSUMPTION | Implied condition with no assumption field |
| CHK-RE-20 | Allocation level matches the subject | CONTRACT-EMV-004 allocated; AC-EMV-009 | inspection | WRONG_LEVEL | Allocation versus subject grain |
