   127	
   128	| ID | Statement | Source | Verification | Allocation |
   129	|---|---|---|---|---|
   130	| AC-AFC-PROF-01 | When the customer starts Yahoo linking on the TV app, the TV app shall display a device code and a link URL, and the backend shall bind the Yahoo authorization the customer completes in a phone browser to that device if it completes within device_code_ttl, and shall store the Yahoo OAuth tokens only in the backend. | #1 item 1, #1 item 6 (device-code linking), SD-005, SD-007 | test, demonstration | M3; DeviceAuth, LineupConnector, ProfileSettings |
   131	| AC-AFC-PROF-02 | When a linked Yahoo account exists, the backend shall list the customer's NFL leagues and teams, and the TV app shall let the customer select teams, individual players and favorite NFL teams; the backend shall classify each roster player as starter, bench or unknown from the roster's selected position for the current NFL week. | #1 item 1, #1 §Source review (Yahoo) | test | M3; LineupConnector, ProfileSettings |
   132	| AC-AFC-PROF-03 | The TV app shall detect which allow-listed packages are installed using the Android package manager, shall show each detected provider app's subscription status as "Unknown" until the customer confirms it, and shall let the customer override the detected apps, each subscription status, and the local market. | #1 item 1, #1 item 4 | test, demonstration | M3; AppDetector, ProfileSettings |
   133	| AC-AFC-PROF-04 | If Yahoo access is not approved at T_yahoo, then the system shall offer manual lineup entry from ESPN team rosters and shall label that lineup "Manual lineup" on every screen and panel that shows it. | SD-007, C6 | test | M3; LineupConnector (ManualSource), ProfileSettings |
   134	
   135	### Product — monitoring and feed (issue #1 item 2)
   136	
   137	| ID | Statement | Source | Verification | Allocation |
   138	|---|---|---|---|---|
   139	| AC-AFC-MON-01 | While a game involving a followed player is in progress and at least one following customer is in an enabled viewing period, the backend shall fetch that game's ESPN summary once every feed_poll_interval, and shall fetch no game that no such customer follows. | #1 item 2, SD-004 | test | M3; FeedIngest |
   140	| AC-AFC-MON-02 | The backend shall fetch each in-progress game at most once per feed_poll_interval regardless of how many customers follow it. | #1 §Lightweight device design (shared ingestion) | test | M3; FeedIngest |
   141	| AC-AFC-MON-03 | The TV app shall read no current-playback context unless the customer has enabled detection; if the device exposes no supported current-playback interface (SP-2 verdict), then the detection setting shall read "Not available on this device"; every alert and panel state not derived from observed playback shall be labeled "Based on your profile". | #1 item 2 | test, inspection | M3; ProfileSettings, AlertNotifier |
   142	| AC-AFC-MON-04 | While the device is outside every enabled viewing period, the TV app shall send no alert long-poll requests. | #1 item 2, #1 §Lightweight device design | test | M3; AlertService |
   143	| AC-AFC-FEED-01 | The backend shall emit GameEvents for ESPN plays and game-state changes that meet the event definitions in DES-AFC-FEED, and for corrections required by AC-AFC-FEED-02, using CONTRACT-AFC-EVENT with source game id, source play id, event type, involved ESPN athlete ids, possession team, field position, period, game clock, source timestamp and ingest timestamp; it shall emit no GameEvent for a play that meets none of those definitions and shall reject a schema-invalid response without changing stored GameEvents. | SD-004, #1 item 3 | test | M3; FeedIngest |
   144	| AC-AFC-FEED-02 | The backend shall emit at most one original GameEvent per source game id and source play id; when the recorded scoring content for that play changes, it shall emit one correction GameEvent for that change referencing the original event, and repeated retrieval of unchanged scoring content shall emit no additional event. | #1 item 3 (duplicates, corrections) | test | M3; FeedIngest |
   145	| AC-AFC-FEED-03 | If one game's ESPN fetch fails or returns a schema-invalid response feed_fail_limit times in a row, then the backend shall mark that game's data stale; when the operator enables replay, the backend shall serve GameEvents from recorded fixtures and every alert and panel value derived from them shall carry the label "Replay — recorded game data". | C2, #1 §Judging (labeled replay) | test | M3; FeedIngest (ReplaySource) |
