    96	
    97	The Kotlin package is `afc.companion`. Paths in committed files are
    98	repository-relative (AC-AFC-PATH-01).
    99	
   100	### Placement mapping (Systems Modeler receipt → design paths)
   101	
   102	`specialists/systems-modeler-receipt.md` lists candidate placements. The
   103	design adopts them with two naming choices: the receipt's `<pkg>` is
   104	`afc/companion` (Kotlin package `afc.companion`), and the receipt's backend
   105	component directories `backend/src/<component>/` live inside one Python
   106	package `backend/src/afc_backend/` (`device_auth` → `auth`, `feed_ingest` →
   107	`feed` with `replay.py`, `lineup` → `lineup`, `matcher` → `match`,
   108	`alert_policy` → `policy`, `provider_resolver` → `resolver`, `panel` →
   109	`panel`, `api` → `api`); replay fixtures are `backend/fixtures/espn/`. The
   110	receipt's profile screen `profile/ProfileSettingsScreen.kt` is the
   111	`settings` package here. D4 and D5 placements are adopted unchanged.
   112	
   113	## Decisions
   114	
   115	### DES-AFC-ARCH — Split of work between TV and backend
   116	
   117	- The backend owns every external fetch (ESPN, Yahoo), identity matching,
   118	  alert policy, provider resolution and fantasy scoring. The TV app owns
   119	  settings input, app detection, notification display, the launch intent and
   120	  the panel rendering. No secret or third-party token reaches the TV app
   121	  (AC-AFC-SEC-01).
   122	- Transport is HTTPS JSON to one API Gateway HTTP API. Alerts reach the TV
   123	  by long-poll (`GET /v1/alerts?wait=` up to alert_poll_wait) only during
   124	  enabled viewing periods (AC-AFC-MON-04). Push through Amazon Device
   125	  Messaging is the documented alternative if SP-2 shows the long-poll service
   126	  does not survive provider playback; adopting it is a class C owner decision
   127	  because it needs an owner developer-console registration.
   128	- Requirements: AC-AFC-MON-02, AC-AFC-MON-04, AC-AFC-SEC-01, AC-AFC-LW-01.
   129	- Lenses: Contract-first, Lightweight TV, Security controls.
   130	
   197	### DES-AFC-PANEL — Lineup panel and panel modes
   198	
   199	- Layout: a horizontal split; the panel takes a fixed 30 % of screen width on
   200	  the right; the video occupies the left 70 % with resize mode FIT, so the
   201	  frame is letterboxed, never cropped or covered (AC-AFC-PANEL-02).
   202	- Mode B candidates for SP-4, tried in this order inside spike_panel_max:
   203	  provider picture-in-picture beside the companion activity; platform
   204	  multi-window; a provider integration exposed by Amazon Builder Tools. A
   205	  system overlay drawn over provider video is rejected by AC-AFC-PANEL-02.
   206	- Mode A: `CompanionPlayer` plays one CC-BY or CC0 clip fetched by
   207	  `tools/fetch-footage.sh` against a pinned sha256 into the git-ignored
   208	  `tv-app/app/src/main/assets/footage/` at build time, so it ships inside the
   209	  debug APK and is never committed (SM F12), with the on-screen label "Sample
   210	  footage — not a live broadcast" (SD-006a).
   211	- Manual-lineup scoring (AC-AFC-PANEL-01): the documented default table is
   212	  `backend/src/afc_backend/panel/default_scoring.json` (passing yard 0.04,
   213	  passing TD 4, interception −1, rushing or receiving yard 0.1, rushing or
   214	  receiving TD 6, reception 0.5, two-point conversion 2, fumble lost −2,
   215	  field goal 3/4/5 by 0–39/40–49/50+ yards, extra point 1; team defense not
   216	  scored and shown "Unavailable"), labeled "Default scoring" wherever shown.
   217	- Data: `/v1/panel` every panel_refresh while visible, and once on show; each value carries
   218	  `fetched_at`; the TV marks values older than stale_after "Stale" and absent
   219	  values "Unavailable" (AC-AFC-PANEL-01). Remote: D-pad left/right moves
   220	  focus between video and panel; a dedicated menu toggles show/hide; team
   221	  and league selection is a focusable list (AC-AFC-PANEL-03).
   222	- Lenses: Device integration, Honest outcomes, Lightweight TV.
   223	
   224	### DES-AFC-FEED — ESPN ingestion
   225	
   226	- `FeedIngest` runs on an EventBridge Scheduler schedule that fires every
   227	  minute only inside NFL game windows; each invocation fetches the
   228	  scoreboard once, then each followed in-progress game's summary every
   229	  feed_poll_interval for up to 60 s (AC-AFC-MON-01, -02).
   230	- Responses are validated against a schema derived from the SP-5 fixtures;
   231	  invalid responses count toward feed_fail_limit and never overwrite stored
   232	  events (AC-AFC-FEED-01, -03).
   233	- Dedupe key `GAME#<game id>` + `PLAY#<play id>`; a changed scoring play
   234	  emits one `correction` GameEvent referencing the original (AC-AFC-FEED-02).
   235	- Red-zone entry: possession team's ball on or inside red_zone_yards of the
   236	  opponent goal line on a play where the previous play was outside it.
   237	  Close game: 4th quarter or overtime with margin ≤ close_game_margin, emitted
   238	  once per game per lead change into that state.
   239	- `ReplaySource` serves `backend/fixtures/espn/` events on a schedule when the
   240	  SAM parameter `ReplayMode` is `on`; every derived alert and panel value
   241	  carries `replay: true` (AC-AFC-FEED-03). No admin endpoint exists.
   242	- Lenses: Data ingestion, Honest outcomes.
   243	
   244	### DES-AFC-LINEUP — Lineup sources
   245	
   246	- CONTRACT-AFC-LINEUPSOURCE has two implementations. `YahooSource` uses
   247	  OAuth 2.0 authorization code with read scope only (AC-AFC-SEC-04), calls
   248	  `/users;use_login=1/games;game_keys=nfl/teams`,
   249	  `/team/{team_key}/roster;week={week}` and `/league/{league_key}/settings`,
   250	  and classifies slots from `selected_position` (AC-AFC-PROF-02).
   251	  `ManualSource` builds a lineup from ESPN team rosters entered on the TV
   252	  (AC-AFC-PROF-04).
   253	- The active source per customer is Yahoo when linked; at T_yahoo, if no
   254	  Yahoo client credential exists in SSM (SP-6 check), ManualSource becomes
   255	  the default and every view labels "Manual lineup" (C6).
   256	- `Matcher` maps Yahoo player keys to ESPN athlete ids by normalized name,
   257	  NFL team and position, with a reviewed override file
   258	  `backend/src/afc_backend/match/overrides.json`; unmatched players show
   259	  "Unmatched" (RISK-AFC-10).
   260	- Lenses: Personalization, Honest outcomes, Security controls.
   261	
   262	### DES-AFC-POLICY — Matching and alert policy
   263	
   264	- Relevance rules of AC-AFC-ALERT-01; policy order: enabled alert type →
   265	  quiet hours → duplicate check (one alert per customer per source event) →
   266	  alert_min_gap per game → spoiler_delay hold → release (AC-AFC-ALERT-02).
   267	- Correction GameEvents release a correction alert and update panel totals
   268	  (AC-AFC-ALERT-03, AC-AFC-PANEL-04).
   269	- Text templates (AC-AFC-ALERT-05): the documented mapping is
   270	  `backend/src/afc_backend/policy/templates.json`, one fixed template set per
   271	  customer-selectable excitement level (`calm`, `standard`, `hype`) and event
   272	  type; substitution inputs are GameEvent fields and matched player data
   273	  only. No
   274	  generative commentary unless the owner selects OD-AFC-02.
   275	- Lenses: Personalization, Honest outcomes.
   276	
   277	### DES-AFC-AUTH — Device linking and tokens
   278	
   279	- `POST /v1/link/start` returns `device_code`, short `user_code`,
   280	  `verify_url`, `expires_in` = device_code_ttl. The phone browser opens
   281	  `verify_url`, enters `user_code`, and is redirected to Yahoo OAuth; the
   282	  callback stores Yahoo tokens under the device's customer record and marks
   283	  the link complete. The TV polls `/v1/link/status` and receives a random
   284	  256-bit device bearer token, stored hashed (SHA-256) in DynamoDB
   285	  (AC-AFC-PROF-01, AC-AFC-SEC-01, -02).
   286	- Manual-lineup customers link without Yahoo: `link/start` then confirm on
   287	  the TV yields a device token with no Yahoo tokens.
   288	- The Yahoo client id and secret live in SSM Parameter Store SecureString
   289	  parameters the owner creates (credential access is owner-only); Lambda
   290	  reads them through its IAM role.
   291	- Yahoo OAuth access and refresh tokens are stored only in the DynamoDB item
   292	  `CUST#<id>#YAHOO` (table encryption at rest), read only by LineupConnector,
   293	  and returned by no API route (AC-AFC-SEC-01). This binds the storage choice
   294	  the Requirements Engineer returned to design: the placement receipt's
   295	  "tokens in SSM SecureString" applies to the client secret only.
   296	- Lenses: Security controls.
   297	
   298	### DES-AFC-INFRA — AWS serverless on the Free plan
   299	
   300	- `backend/template.yaml` is a hot file (SM F5): S05 owns it; a later slice
   406	### DES-AFC-GATE — This repository's gate
   407	
   408	- `tools/ci/gate.sh` implements CONTRACT-AFC-GATE with four areas:
   409	  - `android`: `cd tv-app && ./gradlew --no-daemon :app:lintDebug
   410	    :app:testDebugUnitTest :app:assembleDebug` (paths `tv-app/**`).
   411	  - `backend`: `uv run --project backend --frozen ruff check backend`,
   412	    `uv run --project backend --frozen pytest backend/tests`,
   413	    `uv run --project backend --frozen python backend/tools/check_template.py
   414	    backend/template.yaml` (paths `backend/**`).
   415	  - `spec`: `uv run --script tools/spec/spec_lint.py
   416	    spec/amazon-fantasy-companion/`, `uv run --script
   417	    tools/spec/diagram.py lint spec/amazon-fantasy-companion/`, a
   418	    rebuild and `git diff --exit-code` on the built file (paths `spec/**`,
   419	    `tools/spec/**`). Before S19 vendors `tools/spec/`, the area reports
   420	    `GAP tools/spec missing` only when `spec/**` exists; with neither present
   421	    it reports `PASS nothing to check`.
   422	  - `hygiene`: `python3 tools/ci/check_paths.py` over all tracked files
   423	    (AC-AFC-CI-03, AC-AFC-PATH-01). Documented rule identities:
   424	    `PATH-HOME-POSIX` (`/home/<user>/`), `PATH-HOME-MAC` (`/Users/<user>/`),
   425	    `PATH-HOME-WIN` (`C:\Users\<user>\`), `CRED-AWS-KEY-ID`,
   426	    `CRED-AWS-SECRET`, `CRED-YAHOO-SECRET`, `CRED-OAUTH-TOKEN`,
   427	    `CRED-DEVICE-TOKEN`; each finding prints `file:line:rule-id` and never
   428	    the matched text; placeholder user segments (`user`, `example-user`) are
   429	    allowed plus the D4-B workflow checker over
   430	    `.github/workflows/` (always runs; the checker is vendored into
   431	    `tools/ci/` by S09 from the merged D4-B commit because the shared skill is
   432	    private).
   433	- `.githooks/pre-commit` runs `gate.sh --changed`; `.githooks/pre-push` runs
   434	  `gate.sh --changed` against the merge base with `origin/main`; installed by
   435	  the D4-A installer (`core.hooksPath .githooks`).
   436	- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (AC-AFC-CI-02): `on: pull_request` and `push`
   437	  to `main`; `concurrency: ci-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}` with
   438	  `cancel-in-progress: true`; a `changes` job computes areas with a pinned
   439	  path-filter action; one job per area named `gate / <area>`; every action
   440	  pinned by full SHA; `permissions: contents: read`; `ubuntu-latest`
   441	  GitHub-hosted runners; no secrets referenced; Graphviz installed by apt in
   442	  the `spec` job.
   443	- Lenses: Parallel-safe CI, Security controls.
   444	
   445	### DES-AFC-D4 — Shared CI/CD capability (Alphazedehq)
