# Requirement quality gate

Run this file after authoring and after the NASA-adapted checklist. Do not
author here. Do not merge checklist concerns into the authoring method. Do
not persist SDoc or SysON. Do not choose models or lineups. Do not write
product tests.

Cite S8 rows `SRC-EMV-NASA-SEH`, `SRC-EMV-COE`, and `SRC-EMV-29148`
(metadata-only, no clauses). This gate is a procedure, not a register
(DES-EMV-022, AC-EMV-008).

## Preconditions

- Candidate statement plus the authoring fields from
  [requirements-authoring.md](requirements-authoring.md)
- Checklist file [nasa-requirement-checklist.md](nasa-requirement-checklist.md)
- S8 receipts present
- Request is not persistence, lineup choice, or product-test authoring

If the request is persistence, return `TYPED_GAP_RS_PERSISTENCE` and write
nothing. If it is lineup choice, return `TYPED_GAP_LINEUP`. If it is product
tests, return `TYPED_GAP_TEST_CODE`.

## Procedure

1. Load every `CHK-RE-*` row. Skipping a row is `FAIL` unless the record
   marks `N/A` with a scope reason.
2. For each row, apply the named check type to the candidate and record
   `PASS`, `FAIL`, or `N/A`.
3. On `FAIL`, record the row's typed failure and the evidence string. Do not
   invent a new failure code.
4. On `N/A`, record the reason. A blank reason becomes `FAIL`.
5. Aggregate:
   - `PASS` if every row is `PASS` or justified `N/A`
   - `FAIL` if any row is `FAIL`
6. Return the record below. Hand persistence to Requirements System. Do not
   treat this record as SDoc, review, or publication.

Three correction rounds may re-author and re-check. Stop when the gate
passes, a typed gap applies, S8 is missing, or rounds are exhausted.

## Record

```text
gate: requirements-engineering/quality-gate
candidate_id: <id>
authoring_file: references/requirements-authoring.md
checklist_file: references/nasa-requirement-checklist.md
s8_rows: SRC-EMV-NASA-SEH, SRC-EMV-COE, SRC-EMV-29148
verdict: PASS | FAIL | TYPED_GAP | BLOCKED
typed_failures: <codes or none>
typed_gap: <code or none>
rows:
  - id: CHK-RE-NN
    result: PASS | FAIL | N/A
    typed_failure: <code or none>
    evidence: <observable>
    na_reason: <reason or none>
```

## Typed gaps (not gate failures)

| code | request | owner |
| --- | --- | --- |
| TYPED_GAP_RS_PERSISTENCE | write, revise, validate, review, or publish SDoc/SysON | `use-requirements-system` |
| TYPED_GAP_LINEUP | choose harness, model, or lineup | Bearing Lite |
| TYPED_GAP_TEST_CODE | write product tests | Test Engineering / `write-tests` |
| TYPED_GAP_SKILL_AUTHORING | create or revise a skill | `create-lean-skill` |

interface-completeness-profile.md
## Required fields

| field | topics it must cover | notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `purpose_and_scope` | why the interface exists and what it bounds | |
| `precedence` | which document controls on conflict | |
| `applicable_and_reference_sources` | binding sources versus referenced sources | |
| `endpoint_identities_and_responsibilities` | endpoint identity; responsibilities and ownership per side | |
| `exchanged_data_signals_or_quantities` | exchanges and direction per item | |
| `types_shapes_units_limits_timing_and_protocol` | data types and structure; units and conventions; limits and tolerances; timing and performance; protocol and transport | composite; rule 6 roll-up |
| `initialization_states_errors_and_recovery` | initialization and shutdown; states and modes; errors and fault containment; recovery and resynchronization | composite; rule 6 roll-up |
| `authoritative_requirement_ids` | requirement links into the authority of record | unresolved link → `UNRESOLVED_LINK` |
| `model_relationships_or_selected_mode_disposition` | model links, or the selected modeling mode and why no link exists | unresolved link → `UNRESOLVED_LINK` |
| `positive_and_negative_verification_cases` | verification links; both expectations per applicable obligation | one-sided case → `CASE_WITHOUT_NEGATIVE` |
| `gaps` | the open `GAP` records and what each blocks | |

## Three separate verdicts

Never merge these. Each cites evidence of its own class (RISK-EMV-016).

| verdict | question | admissible evidence | inadmissible |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| structural completeness | does every required field carry a valid disposition? | this profile's field-by-field check record | runtime logs |
| semantic compatibility | do both endpoints' obligations agree in meaning? | both sides' obligations compared field by field | a filled profile, a JSON Schema pass, or a diagram |
| connected runtime evidence | does the assembled interface behave as required? | positive and negative cases run on the exact candidate | a mock, a stub, or a schema pass |

A profile pass is structural completeness only. It is not compatibility and not
runtime proof.

## Responsibility allocation

One bounded input, output, and prohibition per role (DES-EMV-038,
AC-EMV-032). No role holds another's authority.

| role | owns | prohibition |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Requirements Engineering | defines interface obligations and applicability; fills field dispositions | does not represent, persist, test, or assemble |
| SysML Modeling | represents obligations and traces model elements to authoritative requirement IDs in the selected mode | does not change the Journey's `diagram-assisted` mode or `sysml_claim` false; does not become a register |
| Requirements System / SysON | governs authoritative persistence, query behavior, relationships, revisions, review, and publication boundaries | not superseded by this profile |
| Test Engineering | defines positive and negative cases for every `APPLICABLE` obligation | does not design the obligation or accept a mock as the acceptance article |
| Integration Engineering | checks compatibility against both endpoints and exercises the connected interface | does not self-certify or treat a profile pass as runtime proof |
| Plan Integrator | consumes resulting evidence into the existing five planning artifacts | not an entry point for filling this profile |

## Profile check — PROC-INTERFACE-PROFILE-CHECK

Inspect the record field by field and return structural completeness only.

Typed failures: `BLANK_APPLICABLE_VALUE`, `UNJUSTIFIED_NOT_APPLICABLE`,
`INCOMPLETE_GAP_RECORD`, `MULTIPLE_DISPOSITIONS`, `HIDDEN_UNKNOWN`,
`UNRESOLVED_LINK`, `CASE_WITHOUT_NEGATIVE`.

Outcomes: exactly one of `PROFILE_COMPLETE`,
`PROFILE_COMPLETE_WITH_GAPS`, or `PROFILE_INCOMPLETE` with typed failures.

## Fixtures

`FIX-IFACE-01` is the representative application. `FIX-IFACE-02` through
`FIX-IFACE-04` are deliberate check fixtures for the procedure. They are not
interface claims and carry no requirement values of their own.

