r0=(p/'specialists/requirements-engineer-receipt.md').read_text()
prior={m[1]:m[2] for m in re.finditer(r'"'^'"\\| ((?:AC|RISK)-AFC-[A-Z0-9-]+) \\| PASS \\| (.*?) \\|"'$'"',r0,re.M)}
notes={
'AC-AFC-FEED-01':'Exact repair; original, correction and non-triggering play dispositions now agree with FEED-02 and CONTRACT-AFC-EVENT (design L554–556); invalid input preserves stored events.',
'AC-AFC-FEED-02':'Exact repair distinguishes the original event, each changed scoring state and repeated unchanged retrieval; no self-contradicting event-count limit.',
'AC-AFC-ALERT-04':'Exact repair conditions heads-up presentation on the selected setting, suppresses it for panel-only, and removes the misapplied alert_poll_wait latency guarantee.',
'AC-AFC-ALERT-05':'Exact repair: “documented mapping from each customer-selectable excitement level to a fixed template”; DES-AFC-POLICY (design L269–274) names templates.json, calm/standard/hype, the level × event-type mapping and permitted substitution inputs. Template wording is an implementation value; the selection rule is observable without inventing an intensity measure.',
'AC-AFC-PANEL-01':'Exact repair: “a documented default scoring table that specifies each counted statistic and its point coefficient”; DES-AFC-PANEL (design L211–216) names default_scoring.json, supplies coefficients and field-goal bands, and explicitly marks team defense Unavailable. Default, stale and unavailable labels remain binding.',
'AC-AFC-PANEL-03':'Exact repair binds remote interaction and visible focus to the TV app rather than imposing a duty on the customer.',
'AC-AFC-PANEL-04':'Exact repair separates backend update, visible polling and refresh on show; source-fact consistency does not depend on every event producing an alert.',
'AC-AFC-SPIKE-01':'Statement retained; exact allocation names the SP-1 compatibility verdict and TV build configuration; device stop and owner boundaries preserved.',
'AC-AFC-SPIKE-02':'Exact statement and allocation distinguish SP-1..SP-5 at M2 exit from SP-6 at T_yahoo/M3 entry; no schedule contradiction remains.',
'AC-AFC-SEC-01':'Exact repair: “Yahoo OAuth tokens exclusively in backend storage, without returning them to the TV app”; DES-AFC-AUTH (design L288–295) explicitly reconciles the earlier placement constraint: client secret in SSM SecureString, OAuth access/refresh tokens in encrypted DynamoDB CUST#<id>#YAHOO, LineupConnector access only, no API return. CONTRACT-AFC-TABLES L583–587 agrees.',
'AC-AFC-D5-02':'Exact repair limits product-specific operational content while preserving the license, attribution and provenance required by D5-01 and SD-022.',
'AC-AFC-D5-05':'Statement retained; exact allocation names the D5 skill, shared links, hook installer and harness skill configurations across M1/M2.',
'AC-AFC-SPEC-01':'Statement retained; exact allocation names D1 sources, vendored tools and provenance/license records; D5-before-D1 sequence unchanged.',
'AC-AFC-SPEC-02':'Exact repair requires every COE-ASA-001 structural-floor element; Source adds that UID and allocation names D1 sources/build. Native SDoc L292–298 confirms the cited duty.',
'AC-AFC-SPEC-03':'Statement retained; exact allocation names D1 revision 1.0; spike/mode/provider limitations remain inspectable.',
'AC-AFC-PLAN-01':'Statement retained; exact allocation names D2 and M1-entry check without deferring planning until implementation.',
'AC-AFC-PLAN-02':'Statement retained; exact allocation names D3 GitHub milestone records; readback comparison remains the observable.',
'AC-AFC-CI-03':'Exact repair: “documented credential-detection rules for Yahoo client secrets, OAuth tokens, AWS credentials and device tokens”; DES-AFC-GATE (design L422–428) names three home-shape and five credential rule IDs, retains placeholder examples, and defines file:line:rule-id output without matched text. No universal secret-detection claim is made.',
'AC-AFC-VNV-01':'Statement retained; exact allocation names root and area Vnv guidance files.',
'AC-AFC-DX-01':'Statement retained; exact allocation names Lifecycle dispatch/return records and the Scribe log.',
'AC-AFC-DX-02':'Statement retained; exact allocation distinguishes M1 observation log and M5 per-tool summary/friction log.',
'AC-AFC-DX-03':'Statement retained; exact allocation names per-tool summary/friction log; sanitization and submission-rules check remain explicit.',
'AC-AFC-SUB-01':'Statement retained; exact allocation names README and judge-access documentation.',
'AC-AFC-SUB-02':'Statement retained; exact allocation names submission checklist and owner-action records; no protected action is authorized here.',
'AC-AFC-SUB-03':'Statement retained; exact allocation names device clips and storyboard/clip index; replay/sample labels remain explicit.',
'AC-AFC-SUB-04':'Statement retained; exact allocation names clips/submission text; voice claims remain conditional on device verification.',
'AC-AFC-LAND-01':'Statement retained; repaired Source names existing workspace rules and plan sections rather than absent CLAUDE.md; allocation names landing/review/repair/gate records.',
'AC-AFC-REV-01':'Statement retained; exact allocation names Reviewer packets and OCR/Reverify capability/execution records; unavailable runs remain typed gaps.',
'AC-AFC-VIS-01':'Statement retained; exact allocation names screenshots and review records; device-state evidence and privacy boundary remain explicit.',
'AC-AFC-PATH-01':'Statement retained; exact allocation names tracked artifacts and hygiene gate, including planning.',
'RISK-AFC-01':'Exact control and metadata; hardware failure stops device work without purchase or platform switch; SP-1 allocation and inspection are explicit.',
'RISK-AFC-02':'Exact control and metadata; SP-2 failure retains ALERT-04 as unmet pending owner scope decision; panel-only cannot silently satisfy it.',
'RISK-AFC-03':'Exact control and metadata; details/app-home remains a recorded limitation, with WATCH-02 unmet until demonstration or owner amendment.',
'RISK-AFC-04':'Exact control and metadata; bounded Mode B failure selects already-decided Mode A and requires disclosure in submission materials.',
'RISK-AFC-05':'Exact control and metadata; rejection/stale rules, labeled demo replay and owner-only ESPN-terms decision have explicit allocations.',
'RISK-AFC-06':'Exact control and metadata; T_yahoo condition and Manual lineup display obligations agree with PROF-04.',
'RISK-AFC-07':'Exact control and metadata; confirmed-limit-only fallback, frozen capability settings and queue-on-exhaustion preserve owner route intent.',
'RISK-AFC-08':'Exact control and metadata; hosted runs stop at the stated budget, local evidence continues, paid overage requires the owner.',
'RISK-AFC-09':'Exact control and metadata; limit exhaustion stops affected work and non-allow-listed deployment is rejected before mutation; no unauthorized paid-plan change.',
'RISK-AFC-10':'Exact control and metadata; unresolved identity has an explicit Unmatched/no-attribution state and subsequent correction behavior.',
'RISK-AFC-11':'Exact control and metadata; pre-publication block and post-exposure sanitized incident/owner notification are distinct responses.',
'RISK-AFC-12':'Exact control and metadata; missing pre-tool hook stays a typed gap and local git hooks cannot substitute for harness integration; AGY lint flag is inapplicable platform-neutrality advice.',
'RISK-AFC-13':'Exact control and metadata; acquisition scan and pinned Gradle checksum precede first use; BLOCK/INDETERMINATE fail closed.',
'RISK-AFC-14':'Exact control and metadata; labeled replay does not satisfy the separate M3 simultaneous-live-games obligation.',
'RISK-AFC-15':'Exact control and metadata; D5 trigger repair is required, reciprocal skill edit remains conditional on OD-AFC-07 at integrated review.',
'RISK-AFC-16':'Exact control and metadata; D5 delay leaves D1/M2 exit unmet until delivery and cannot revive superseded SD-013.'
}
