# Amazon Fantasy Companion — Technical Plan

## Outcome

A customer-configurable Fire TV companion, built for the Amazon Developer
Hackathon Fire TV track and the AWS Builder mini challenge (SD-008), that
notices NFL moments relevant to the viewer's fantasy starters, alerts the
viewer while another viewing app plays, helps the viewer reach the game in a
provider app the viewer already uses, and shows a right-side lineup panel
beside unobscured video. It retains experience items 1, 2, 3, 4 and 6 of
issue #1 plus the right-side panel, and excludes every messaging and
community feature. It runs on the owner's 2018 Fire TV stick on Fire OS from
the `AmazonAppDev/hello-world-fire-tv` starter (SD-001, SD-003), reads live
NFL data from ESPN's unofficial public JSON (SD-004), reads lineups from Yahoo
or, from T_yahoo without approval, from labeled manual entry (SD-007), and
runs its backend on an owner-created AWS Free-plan account (SD-005). The panel
route is decided by a spike bounded by spike_panel_max; on failure the panel
runs beside the app's own player with labeled open-licensed footage (Mode A,
SD-006, SD-006a).

This Lifecycle also delivers (SD-012, SD-016, SD-021):

- **D1** the product architecture specification, written after approval with
  the D5 shared spec-authoring skill (SD-022, which supersedes SD-013);
- **D2** this program plan to T_deadline with parallel waves and milestone
  definitions;
- **D3** the GitHub milestones, created by the Orchestrator after approval;
270:| RISK-AFC-01 | If the stick cannot be located, its API level is below min_sdk, its OS is Fire OS 5 or older, or the provider apps cannot run, then the program shall stop device work and record the condition for the owner without purchasing a device or switching platforms. | SD-001, SD-003, C1, AC-AFC-SPIKE-01 | inspection | M2; SP-1 device compatibility verdict and device-work entry control | The stick cannot be found, is Fire OS 5 or older, is below min_sdk, or cannot run the provider apps. | Stop device work and return to the owner; never buy or switch platforms on the owner's behalf. |
271:| RISK-AFC-02 | If SP-2 cannot demonstrate a heads-up notification over provider playback, then the program shall record the exact device and route limitation, retain panel-only presentation, and record AC-AFC-ALERT-04 as unmet pending an owner scope decision. | #1 Development setup, AC-AFC-ALERT-04 | inspection | M2; SP-2 notification verdict and AlertNotifier; M3; integration acceptance record | Fire OS on the stick does not show a heads-up notification over a provider app's playback. | Record the exact limitation; panel-only presentation remains; owner scope decision (class C). |
272:| RISK-AFC-03 | If SP-3 finds no supported content-level link for a specific game, then the program shall record the verified details-page or app-home outcome and its limitation, prepare the missing-interface proposal for the owner, and retain AC-AFC-WATCH-02 as unmet until a specific-game route is demonstrated or the owner changes its acceptance condition. | #1 App launch and game/channel routing research, AC-AFC-WATCH-01, AC-AFC-WATCH-02 | inspection | M2; SP-3 provider-route verdict and ProviderResolver registry; M3; WatchLauncher integration acceptance record | No provider exposes a content-level deep link the companion can invoke for a specific game. | Ship the best verified outcome (details or app home), state the limitation, and record the missing interface as an integration proposal for the owner. |
273:| RISK-AFC-04 | If SP-4 fails to verify Mode B within spike_panel_max, then the system shall use Mode A under AC-AFC-PANEL-05 and the submission materials shall state that the panel is beside the companion’s sample footage rather than provider playback. | SD-006, SD-006a, C5, AC-AFC-PANEL-05 | inspection, demonstration | M2; SP-4 verdict; M3; CompanionPlayer/LineupPanel; M5; submission materials | No supported route places the panel beside a provider app's video. | Mode A with labeled footage; limitation stated in the submission. |
274:| RISK-AFC-05 | If ESPN responses become unavailable or schema-invalid, then the backend shall apply the rejection and stale-data rules of AC-AFC-FEED-01 and AC-AFC-FEED-03 and use labeled replay for the affected demo segments; the submission checklist shall retain the ESPN-terms decision as an owner-only action. | SD-004, C2, C3, AC-AFC-FEED-01, AC-AFC-FEED-03, AC-AFC-SUB-02 | test, inspection | M3; FeedIngest/ReplaySource; M5; submission checklist and demo material | ESPN's unofficial endpoints change, rate-limit or go down. | Switch to labeled replay for the demo; owner decides ESPN terms at submission (C3). |
275:| RISK-AFC-06 | If Yahoo access is not approved at T_yahoo, then the system shall provide manual lineup entry from ESPN rosters and label every display of that lineup “Manual lineup” under AC-AFC-PROF-04. | SD-007, C6, AC-AFC-PROF-04 | test | M3; LineupConnector (ManualSource), ProfileSettings and LineupPanel | Yahoo access is not approved by T_yahoo. | Labeled manual lineup. |
276:| RISK-AFC-07 | If a selected route reaches a confirmed usage or rate limit, then the Orchestrator shall record the limit evidence and activate only the next approved fallback in the frozen profile with a class B receipt preserving the selected coverage-assist and Reverify settings, or queue the slice when no approved fallback remains; other invocation, configuration, authentication or runtime errors shall not trigger a route switch. | DEC-AFC-PROFILE-001, frozen profile fallback order, owner route-preservation instructions | inspection | M1–M5; frozen lifecycle binding, dispatch packets and route-activation receipts | A frozen route's usage window is exhausted mid-wave (observed: Muse HTTP 429 on 2026-10-11, reset 2026-10-12T00:00:00Z). | Activate the next approved fallback; queue the slice when all are exhausted. |
277:| RISK-AFC-08 | If private-repository Actions usage exhausts gh_private_minutes, then the program shall stop hosted workflow runs and retain local gate evidence without enabling paid overage unless the owner authorizes it. | SD-017, C11, AC-AFC-CI-02 | inspection | M1–M5; GitHub Actions workflow/budget control and repo gate evidence | Actions minutes on the private repository run out (C11). | Hosted runs stop; local gate evidence continues; no paid overage without the owner. |
278:| RISK-AFC-09 | If the AWS Free-plan limits or credits are exhausted or a deployment would introduce a resource outside AC-AFC-SEC-03, then the program shall stop the affected scheduled work or reject that deployment before a change, and shall make no paid-plan change without the owner’s decision. | SD-005, C4, AC-AFC-SEC-03 | test, inspection | M2–M5; backend infrastructure deployment guard and EventBridge scheduler control | AWS Free-plan limits or credits are reached, or a paid resource is introduced (C4). | Stop the scheduler; owner decides any plan change. |
279:| RISK-AFC-10 | If the Matcher cannot establish a Yahoo-to-ESPN player identity, then the system shall label that player “Unmatched” and withhold player-attributed points and alerts until a verified mapping is available; when a mapping correction changes an already released player attribution, it shall apply the correction to the affected alert and panel state. | #1 item 3 and Right-side fantasy lineup panel; DES-AFC-LINEUP; AC-AFC-ALERT-03 | test | M3; Matcher identity map and LineupPanel; M4; AlertPolicy/PanelService corrections | Yahoo and ESPN player identities mismatch, so alerts miss or misattribute a player. | Manual mapping override in the identity map; correction alert. |
